emplate.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":106,"oldLines":3,"newStart":106,"newLines":4,"lines":[" - 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-316, TC-321). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."," - 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: test-cases.toml (ref: WI-834). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."," - 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: system-requirements.toml (re-attested: SR-046, SR-237); low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-047, LLR-270, LLR-300, LLR-301). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes.","+- 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (ref: WI-834); test-cases.toml (ref: WI-834). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":512,"oldLines":3,"newStart":512,"newLines":9,"lines":[" date = \"2026-10-09\""," approved = []"," reattested = [\"LLR-047\", \"LLR-270\", \"LLR-300\", \"LLR-301\", \"SR-046\", \"SR-237\"]","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 85","+date = \"2026-10-09\"","+approved = [\"LLR-316\", \"LLR-317\", \"LLR-318\", \"LLR-319\", \"LLR-320\", \"LLR-321\", \"LLR-322\", \"TC-335\", \"TC-336\", \"TC-337\", \"TC-338\", \"TC-339\", \"TC-343\", \"TC-344\", \"TC-345\"]","+reattested = []"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3357,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3357,"newLines":7,"lines":[" detail = \"blackout_at is the sole reader of the declared blackout value. At a supplied or current UTC instant it returns the declared value, whether the instant is inside an enabled interval, that interval's exclusive end, and the most recent interval end at or before the instant. It treats absent, malformed and equal endpoints as disabled, starts intervals only on weekdays, and assigns a midnight-wrapping interval to its start weekday.\""," rationale = \"One time interpretation prevents claim, launch, wait and retention paths from disagreeing at a boundary or after a policy edit.\""," test_refs = \"TC-335\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3369,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3369,"newLines":7,"lines":[" detail = \"act reads the blackout decision before building, accounting, recording or launching a call. During a window it admits only an ADJUDICATE call carrying a work item whose primary-checkout registry claim is active; every other call raises BlackoutRefused and releases any retained lease. through_blackout waits for a refusal's end and retries the caller's attempt.\""," rationale = \"The one launch boundary keeps callers from bypassing the pause while retaining the wrap-up exception.\""," test_refs = \"TC-336\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3381,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3381,"newLines":7,"lines":[" detail = \"wait_out_blackout obtains its current interval from blackout_at, waits exactly to the exclusive end when inside one, and otherwise returns. Every loop launch, interactive call and recovery probe routes a blackout refusal through through_blackout, so a pre-window lane remains claimed and retries only after the window.\""," rationale = \"The loop needs an explicit wait policy because a launch refusal alone would turn a temporary pause into a failed unattended run.\""," test_refs = \"TC-337\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3393,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3393,"newLines":7,"lines":[" detail = \"claim_work refuses a new assignment while blackout_at reports an active window, naming its end. run retains an assignment claimed before the interval, waits through an idle blackout without spinning or ending it, and resumes the normal poll after the interval.\""," rationale = \"A dispatcher pause must preserve already assigned work while preventing an assignment that can only sit idle.\""," test_refs = \"TC-338\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3405,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3405,"newLines":7,"lines":[" detail = \"The --for-run/-ForRun operation reports workstation readiness first, then offers each missing setup item only at an interactive terminal; without one it offers nothing and does not consume menu input. It exits 0 when the runtime is ready after the offers and otherwise exits 1 with the step to take. The standalone --check/-Check operation reports only, performs no offer or write, and exits 0.\""," rationale = \"A menu can be useful only after its runtime is usable, but the readiness step must not turn a piped or automated launch into an unattended installer.\""," test_refs = \"TC-343\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-009\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3417,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3417,"newLines":7,"lines":[" detail = \"The workstation report omits the retained-adjudicator sign-in item while retention is off; otherwise it reports signed-in only for a readable configured token, missing when the token cannot be read, and unknown when no suitable runtime can obtain the reading while continuing the rest of the report. It never prints or stores the token.\""," rationale = \"A dedicated retained-session home cannot be made usable by an operator who cannot distinguish a missing credential from an unreadable environment, while reporting must not disclose that credential.\""," test_refs = \"TC-344\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-009\""," phase = 6"," "]},{"oldStart":3429,"oldLines":6,"newStart":3429,"newLines":6,"lines":[" detail = \"When the shipped coordinator-hook example declares guard hooks and the current settings leave them off, an interactive consent may enable them by merging the guard hooks into the settings while preserving existing hooks and unrelated settings. A declined offer changes neither configuration nor credentials, and an example with no guard hooks creates no settings change.\""," rationale = \"Coordinator hooks change a contributor's interactive environment, so an explicit opt-in preserves existing configuration and leaves a declined setup reversible.\""," test_refs = \"TC-345\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-009\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3405,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3405,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"The end is exclusive, last_end is inclusive, only weekday-start intervals exist, disabled values answer neither question, and each call reads the current declaration.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_end_minute_is_exclusive_and_the_last_end_inclusive; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_friday_night_window_runs_into_saturday; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_sunday_night_window_does_not_exist; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_disabled_window_answers_neither_question; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_changed_value_applies_from_the_next_call; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_window_function_is_the_only_reader_of_the_dial\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-336]"]},{"oldStart":3416,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3416,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"Only an active-claim adjudication launches in the interval; a refused call records nothing and the loop retries after the window. A refused retained call releases its lease before BlackoutRefused.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_non_adjudication_launch_is_refused_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_an_adjudication_without_an_active_claim_is_refused; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_wrap_up_adjudication_of_an_active_claim_launches; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_refused_call_records_nothing; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_loop_waits_out_a_refused_launch_and_resumes_after_it; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_wrap_up_verdict_asking_for_rework_leaves_the_rework_waiting; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_review_next_or_rework_launch_is_refused_for_an_active_claim; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_refused_retained_call_releases_its_lease\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-337]"]},{"oldStart":3427,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3427,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"The loop waits only while inside the interval, and each of its three refusal routes retries its eligible launch once after the window.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_loops_pre_session_wait_asks_the_window_function; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_loop_waits_out_a_refused_launch_and_resumes_after_it; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_each_loop_route_waits_out_a_refused_launch_and_retries\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-338]"]},{"oldStart":3438,"oldLines":18,"newStart":3438,"newLines":18,"lines":[" expected = \"A new dispatcher claim refuses inside the window and an earlier assignment waits then resumes.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_dispatchers_claim_is_refused_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_dispatcher_holds_its_claim_and_waits_out_an_idle_window\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-339]"," verifies = [\"SR-229\", \"LLR-300\", \"IF-271\", \"IF-274\", \"IF-275\", \"SR-237\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Exercise claims and hooks during blackout with the context guard off. Exercise quote-aware shell reading, expandable and literal here bodies, and unreadable-line denial. Assert SessionStart and monitored events provide the close-down instruction at the first window event and every twentieth thereafter, and that the route registry supplies model-CLI names.\"","+method = \"Exercise claims and hooks during blackout with the context guard off. Exercise quote-aware shell reading, expandable and literal here bodies, and unreadable-line denial. Assert every SessionStart inside a window provides the close-down instruction and, for each main session, its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter provide it; assert that the route registry supplies model-CLI names.\""," tier = \"Smoke\"","-expected = \"Claims refuse on both routes and hooks deny only declared main-session launch forms. Quote-aware words and expandable bodies that launch a model are denied; quoted bodies are allowed; unreadable shell input is denied. The close-down instruction names each lane's handoff obligation at that cadence, and model-CLI names follow the route registry. It also instructs no relaunch before the session ends.\"","+expected = \"Claims refuse on both routes and hooks deny only declared main-session launch forms. Quote-aware words and expandable bodies that launch a model are denied; quoted bodies are allowed; unreadable shell input is denied. The close-down instruction appears at every SessionStart inside a window and, for each main session, at its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter; it names each lane's handoff obligation, instructs no relaunch before the session ends, and model-CLI names follow the route registry.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_claim_inside_the_window_is_refused_with_the_guard_off; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_dispatchers_claim_is_refused_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hooks_deny_each_launch_form_with_the_guard_off; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hooks_allow_everything_else; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_subagents_call_is_never_denied; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_quoted_launch_form_is_denied; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_quoted_operator_is_not_a_command_boundary; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_an_unreadable_command_line_is_denied_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_one_reading_keeps_quoted_text_in_its_word; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_json_array_template_names_its_cli; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_session_start_and_the_monitored_events_tell_the_close_down; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_cli_names_come_from_the_route_registry\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-340]"]},{"oldStart":3493,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3493,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"The operation reports before offering, offers nothing without a terminal, preserves piped menu input, and exits with guidance when the runtime remains missing; standalone check is read-only and exits 0. At a terminal each missing item is offered consent-first, while standalone check offers and writes nothing.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_terminal_each_missing_item_is_offered_consent_first; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_standalone_check_at_a_terminal_offers_and_writes_nothing\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-344]"]},{"oldStart":3504,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3504,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"The sign-in item is off when retention is off, otherwise reports signed-in, missing, or unknown accurately while the rest of the report remains available and no token is disclosed. The token is neither printed nor stored.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_sign_in_is_reported_signed_in_missing_or_off; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_sign_in_reads_unknown_without_a_runtime; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_powershell_check_reports_the_sign_in; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_sign_in_reading_is_off_while_retention_is_off; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_sign_in_reading_names_signed_in_and_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_sign_in_report_never_prints_or_stores_the_token\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-345]"]},{"oldStart":3515,"oldLines":5,"newStart":3515,"newLines":5,"lines":[" expected = \"Consent enables the coordinator hooks by preserving existing settings and hooks; denial changes no configuration or credential; and an example without guard hooks changes nothing.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_denial_changes_no_configuration_or_credential; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_hooks_command_reports_and_switches_on; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_merges_and_keeps_existing_hooks; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hook_opt_in_with_no_guard_hooks_changes_nothing\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsAVippwLTQQN229sCyt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sitting 008 clears the lane's spine: all six amended rows are re-anchored and all 15 rows are approved. There are three commits: the verdict (`56746235`), the re-attestation (`5351d867`) and the approval (`57a8fa51`). Each ends with `WI: WI-834` and passed the commit hooks.\n\n**What changed and what I checked:** the lane's answering commit `ff1d291e` changed only the three cells sitting 007 returned, and no code.\n- **LLR-300 and TC-339** now say what the hooks actually do: the close-down instruction comes at every SessionStart in a window, and on each main session's 1st, 21st, 41st… monitored event, counted per session per window. I read this against `coordinator_guard.py`.\n- **SR-237** ties \"without retaining a session whose prior use predates that window's end\" back to the resume after the window. It no longer forbids the wrap-up resume inside the window that SR-227 allows.\n- I re-ran the blackout and run/dev-setup suites: `93 passed, 4 skipped`. The skips are the same four as last time: one POSIX-only test and three that need a terminal this Windows host doesn't have.\n\n**amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=6`.** SR-046, LLR-047, LLR-270, LLR-300 and LLR-301 change meaning. SR-237 is only a clarity change against its approved wording:\n- the wrap-up adjudication is still a permitted exception;\n- \"starting no model work\" restates \"pause new model work\";\n- dropping \"already\" changes nothing, because no claim can be made inside a window.\n\nI blessed and re-attested all six. That anchors the SR and LLR registry copies that sittings 006 and 007 could not take.\n\n**first-approval: `OUTCOME: APPROVE rows=15`.** I approved and flipped LLR-316 to LLR-322, TC-335 to TC-339 and TC-343 to TC-345. A TOML parse confirmed that only those 15 Status cells changed. The scoped snapshot ran without refusal.\n\nThe `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":402470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881},"output_tokens":705,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"bb3d229a-df53-4063-9674-13e3beb1cdfd","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:49:45.362Z","request_id":"req_011CfsAViZDUcEG8w9YoEHKf"}
